Underlying public electoral, geographic and demographic data obtained from the
Brazilian Superior Electoral Court (TSE), IBGE and other public sources are not
covered by this reservation and remain subject to the terms of their sources.
Votes, percentages, precinct counts and other results released by the electoral
authority are public facts, and nothing here purports to restrict access to
them or their reproduction from the official source.

Distinct from the underlying facts is the ElectoMaps database, whose selection
and organization constitute an intellectual creation protected under article 7,
item XIII, and article 87 of Brazilian Law No. 9.610/1998. That protection
covers the curatorial work, not the underlying facts. It includes, among other
elements: the reconstruction of results for municipalities created after the
election in question, derived by aggregating electoral precincts identified in
the earliest election in which the municipality appears, and the corresponding
reattribution of votes from the originating municipalities; the concordance and
normalization tables for municipality names across spellings, codes and
historical territorial divisions; the digitization and structuring of pre-1998
results from unstructured documents; the geocoding of polling places; derived
indices, aggregations and estimates, including the Socioeconomic Index (ISE),
inter-election swing measures and ecological inference estimates; and the
selection, scope, nomenclature, file structure and arrangement of the
collection.

Extraction or reuse of that database, in whole or in substantial part, by any
means, including automated collection, requires prior written permission. This
does not restrict obtaining the underlying public data from its own sources.

Third-party libraries used by the site (including MapLibre GL JS, D3.js, sql.js
and unzipit) remain governed by their own licenses.

